              "slug": "your-brand-vs-tasklane",
              "title": "Your Brand vs Tasklane",
              "kind": "comparison",
              "markdown": "Your Brand and Tasklane both plan and track team work, but they make different trade-offs. This comparison puts the facts side by side, with the date each one was checked.\n\n## Our verdict\n\nPick Your Brand when you want timelines and planning on every plan without a long setup. Pick Tasklane when its strengths in the table above matter more to your team than the gaps. Neither is right for everyone, and the table shows where each one wins.\n\n## Why teams switch\n\nTeams usually move for one reason that shows up in the table: a missing capability, a plan that costs more than expected, or a tool that is heavier than the work needs.\n\n## How to switch\n\n1. Export your projects from Tasklane as CSV.\n2. Import the file into Your Brand from Settings, then check the columns it mapped.\n3. Recreate any automations by hand; they do not transfer between tools.\n4. Invite your team and run both side by side for a week.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Is Your Brand cheaper than Tasklane?\n\nIt depends on the plan and the number of seats; the pricing section above shows both, converted to a monthly figure per seat.\n\n### Can I move my data from Tasklane to Your Brand?\n\nYes for projects and tasks, through a CSV export and import. Automations and comments do not carry across.\n\n## How we compared\n\nEvery fact comes from the vendor's own documentation or pricing page, linked in the sources, and carries the date it was last checked. Scores are not shown.\n",
              "metadata": {
